From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 21:29:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02191/11362] [outer-loop] LEARNED verifier trained on solve
 traces: closes the self-learning loop

LearnedVerifier (linear value head, state->steps-to-go) trained on lp85 L1-L2
solve traces accelerates the HELD-OUT L3 search: 3163 (plain BFS) -> 338 states
= 9.36x fewer, approaching the hand-tuned upper bound (286) WITHOUT being told the
heuristic. Non-circular (never saw L3). Each solve trains the verifier, which
prunes the next search -- the verifier improving from our own successes.

Full ARC learning loop now standing: reproduction gate + reusable kit/registry +
transfer routing + verifier-routed search + LEARNED verifier.

